Starvation Debugging
Answer
Queue Structure
Q1 → Interactive (Highest Priority)

Q2 → System

Q3 → Batch (FCFS)

P5 belongs to Q3
Debug Analysis
Process P5 is in the Q3 (Batch) queue.
The scheduler always executes processes in Q1 first, followed by Q2.
Since new interactive and system processes keep arriving, Q3 is never selected.
As a result, P5 keeps waiting indefinitely and never gets CPU time.
Root Cause
Q1 (Interactive)
        ↓
Executed First
        ↓
Q2 (System)
        ↓
Executed Next
        ↓
P5 in Q3
        ↓
Keeps Waiting
        ↓
Starvation
Optimization

Use Aging

Gradually increase the priority of a process that has been waiting for a long time.
Eventually, P5 is promoted to a higher-priority queue and gets CPU time.
Result
Starvation Eliminated

Fair CPU Scheduling

All Processes Receive CPU Time
